 "sentences": [
  "A defendant once demanded a trial by battle.",
  "In 1817, Abraham Thornton faced a private appeal after being acquitted of murder.",
  "Thornton claimed his medieval right to trial by battle.",
  "The court ruled this was a permissible legal option.",
  "However, the victim's brother declined to fight.",
  "Thornton was freed in 1818.",
  "Parliament abolished these appeals and the right to battle by 1819."
